        <UserObject label="Session isolation (which conversation is which). build_session_key() in session.py:871 deterministically maps every incoming message to a logical session key like agent:main:telegram:dm:12345 or agent:main:slack:channel:C99:U42. It encodes platform + chat type + chat id + (optionally) thread and user id. That means a Telegram DM, a Slack channel, and a WhatsApp group each get distinct keys, so their conversation history, cached agent, and context never bleed into each other. Multi-tenant &quot;profiles&quot; add a further namespace prefix." link="Session isolation (which conversation is which). build_session_key() in session.py:871 deterministically maps every incoming message to a logical session key like agent:main:telegram:dm:12345 or agent:main:slack:channel:C99:U42. It encodes platform + chat type + chat id + (optionally) thread and user id. That means a Telegram DM, a Slack channel, and a WhatsApp group each get distinct keys, so their conversation history, cached agent, and context never bleed into each other. Multi-tenant &quot;profiles&quot; add a further namespace prefix." id="ku3NH2LDfBgmaNuzSJCv-5">
